    "faq": {
      "type": "eis-faq-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "question-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who is it for?",
            "answer": "<p>EIS Pain Relief Oil is for anyone who wants relief from everyday aches and stiffness — people with knee, back, joint, neck or muscle pain, those who spend all day on their feet or sitting, and older parents whose stiffness has started slowing them down. It’s also great even if you don’t have pain — just to unwind and relax tight, tired muscles at the end of the day, and it works well for gym and workout recovery to ease soreness after training.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why do I need EIS Pain Relief Oil?",
            "answer": "<p>If balms, sprays or painkillers only relieve your pain for an hour before it comes back, it’s because they sit on the surface of the skin. EIS is a medicated Ayurvedic oil that absorbs deeper, carrying 15+ herbs into the stiff, aching area so it eases the pain closer to the source instead of just masking it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s actually in it?",
            "answer": "<p>15+ Ayurvedic herbs in a sesame and Mahanarayan oil base — including Nirgundi, Rasna, Ashwagandha, Nilgiri (eucalyptus), Pudina and Gandhapura. No chemicals. It’s an Ayurvedic proprietary medicine for external use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How and when do I use it?",
            "answer": "<p>Warm a little oil, apply it to the affected area, and massage gently in circular motions for 5–10 minutes. Most people use it before bed, and it works well after a workout too. Daily use gives the best results.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer Cash on Delivery?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — Cash on Delivery is available across India, along with UPI, cards and other payment options.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I trust paying online?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely, and here is exactly why you can.</p><p>Our payment gateway is RBI verified. No store in India can process online payments without clearing strict verification and security checks first, so the fact that we can accept prepaid orders means we have already passed them. Every transaction runs through fully encrypted, secure banking channels.</p><p>You are also never alone after you order. We have a real, responsive customer support team that actually replies, ready to help with anything before, during, or after your purchase.</p><p>And paying online genuinely works in your favour. You unlock an extra ₹100 off as a thank you for confirming your order, which is our way of rewarding the customers who help a small business run smoothly. Lower price, full protection, and real humans behind the screen if you ever need us.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it greasy or sticky? Will it stain my sheets?",
            "answer": "<p>No. EIS is light on the skin and absorbs quickly without a greasy or sticky feeling, so it’s comfortable to apply before bed. It also has a soft, herbal aroma — not a harsh chemical smell.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How soon will I feel a difference?",
            "answer": "<p>Many people feel the stiffness loosen within a few minutes of massaging it in. For deeper, lasting relief from chronic stiffness, best results come with consistent nightly use over 2–4 weeks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which types of pain does it help with?",
            "answer": "<p>It’s used for knee pain, back pain, joint pain, muscle pain, neck and shoulder stiffness, leg pain, gym and workout soreness, and everyday aches from standing, sitting or physical work.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it safe for daily use and for elderly people?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — it’s for external use only and gentle enough for regular daily use, which is why many families keep it for their parents. If you have sensitive skin, do a small patch test first. Avoid contact with eyes, nose and mouth, and don’t apply on wounds or broken skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can diabetics or people on medication use it?",
            "answer": "<p>It’s applied externally on the skin and isn’t taken internally. As with any product, if you have a medical condition or are unsure, check with your doctor before use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this the genuine EIS product?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — when you order directly here, you receive the authentic EIS Ayurvedic Pain Relief Oil, made in small batches in a GMP-certified facility and lab-tested for quality.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-13": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if it doesn’t work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>EIS is backed by our money-back guarantee. If you don’t feel a difference, contact us and we’ll make it right.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-14": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does one bottle last?",
            "answer": "<p>Each bottle is 200ml. With regular nightly use on one or two areas, a bottle typically lasts several weeks. Many customers order the multi-bottle pack so they don’t run out or for other family members.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
